# Pure Functions → Helpers

Place **pure functions** (no DB, no HTTP, no env reads, no mutable state) in `src/helpers/`, not in `application/`, `http/`, or mixed into route handlers.

## Put in `src/helpers/`

- Case transforms, string/date/format utilities
- Validation, parsing, chunking, mapping, and deterministic transforms
- Small pure builders with no I/O

Import from `@helpers` (export via `src/helpers/index.ts`).

## Keep elsewhere

| Layer | Responsibility |
|-------|----------------|
| `application/` | Use cases, orchestration, side effects |
| `infrastructure/` | Supabase, external APIs, repositories |
| `http/` | Routes, middleware, request/response |
| `ai/graphs/` | LangGraph nodes and agent wiring |
| `domain/` | Types and domain models |

Domain-specific pure logic used only by one AI module (e.g. `chunk-text.ts`) may live next to that module; **prefer `helpers/`** when the function is generic or reused across layers.

## When editing

- **New pure utility** → add to `src/helpers/`, export from `index.ts`
- **Pure function inside a route or use case** → extract to `helpers/` if reusable or > few lines
- **Do not** duplicate pure logic in `application/` when it belongs in `helpers/`

## Examples

```ts
// ✅ helpers/case-transform.ts
export const keysToCamel = <T>(value: unknown): T => { ... };

// ✅ application/ingest-knowledge-document.ts
import { chunkDocumentText } from '@ai/retrieval/chunk-text.js'; // or @helpers if moved

// ❌ http/routes/knowledge.routes.ts
const normalizeFileName = (name: string) => name.trim().toLowerCase(); // inline — extract to helpers
```

```ts
// ✅ helpers — env-free validation
export const isWithinByteLimit = (bytes: number, max: number): boolean => bytes > 0 && bytes <= max;

// ❌ helpers — reads process.env (side effect)
export const getMaxBytes = () => Number(process.env.KNOWLEDGE_MAX_FILE_BYTES);
// → keep env resolution in config/env.ts; pass values into pure helpers
```
